-- title:
--   Smoothness and geometric connectedness of the generic fibres
-- statement:
--   The data are as follows.
--
--   Arithmetic data. A nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree, two primes $q$ and $q'$ with $q \nmid N$, $q' \nmid N$, $q' \neq q$, both at least $5$, and a nonzero natural number $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$. Further, a valuation subring $A_2$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A₂.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A_2$, together with the assumption (as a `Fact`) that $A_2$ is decomposition-isometric over $\mathbb{Q}$: every element of the decomposition subgroup preserves the valuation of $A_2$. A height-one prime $v_2$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{Z}$ with $q \in v_2$.
--
--   Definite quaternionic data. Rationals $a_1, b_1$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ is definite ($a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$) and division exactly at $q'$, i.e. a finite place $v$ has $\mathbb{H} \otimes \mathbb{Q}_v$ a division algebra precisely when $q' \in v$. Submodules $\Lambda_1, R_1 \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$), and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$. A finite idele $n_1$ lying in the prime Hecke set `primeHeckeSet R₁ q`, such that the order `meetOrder R₁ n₁` $= R_1 \cap R_1^{n_1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq$ (hypothesis `hS₁`), is normalised by $n_1$ (hypothesis `hnorm₁`), and such that shifting twice by $n_1$ is the identity on the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of `meetOrder R₁ n₁` (hypothesis `hsq₁`); the two relevant class sets are finite. The hypothesis `hlaws₁` is `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q Λ₁ R₁ n₁`: the edge Hecke matrices commute with one another, the vertex Hecke matrices commute with one another, away from $q$ the two degeneracy maps intertwine edge and vertex Hecke operators, and the joint kernel of the degeneracy maps is stable under all edge Hecke operators.
--
--   Indefinite quaternionic data and the moduli problem. Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the places above $q$ and $q'$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ in it. A field $F$ (`Fbar`) which is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors exist and have degree $0$, residue fields are finite over the base, and $\Omega_{F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type. A scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ (the localisation away from $D$), a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point `sbar` of that base, and a point-assignment `pt` attaching to each fake elliptic curve for $(\Lambda,N)$ over a ring $S$ a morphism over the structure map; the four hypotheses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` state that `pt` is constant on isomorphism classes, compatible with base change along ring maps and pullback of fake elliptic curves, and, over algebraically closed fields, surjective onto points and injective up to isomorphism.
--
--   Model, Galois and tower data. A curve model $\mathfrak{M}$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an isomorphism $e_\mathfrak{M}$ from $\mathfrak{M}.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along `sbar` with $e_{\mathfrak M}$ followed by the second projection equal to $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{toBase}$, a homomorphism `gal` from $\operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to the semilinear automorphisms of $F$, tower data $\mathbb{T}$ over $F$ indexed by the primes $\ell \neq q, q'$, semilinear Galois actions `galT` on each $\mathbb{T}.F(\ell)$, two semilinear involutive data $W$ and $WT$ indexed by `Fin 2`, and a witness `tw` of type `ModuliTowerWitnessD` for all of these, which records the moduli interpretation of the places of $F$ and of the $\mathbb{T}.F(\ell)$ together with their Galois and Atkin–Lehner compatibilities.
--
--   Local data at $q$. An injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_2$ from $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ into $2\times 2$ matrices over the rational closure of $A_2$ inside the completion of $A_2$ for its valuation, the induced projective representation $\rho_2$ on units (hypothesis $h\rho_2$), a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_2$ whose image in the completion is $q$ (hypothesis $h\varpi_2$), and the assumption that the holomorphic ring `HolRingOf ϖ₂ ρ₂` is a domain.
--
--   Hecke-set and unit-group data. Functions $s_2$ and $sf_2$ on the primes $\ell \neq q, q'$ with values in the units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ and of its finite adelisation, such that, for each $\ell$: $sf_2(\ell)$ has component $s_2(\ell)$ at every place not above $q$ and component $1$ at the places above $q$; the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise; and $\operatorname{nrd}(s_2(\ell)) = \ell$. Subgroups $\Gamma_2$ indexed by `Option` of those primes, with $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ the subgroup of elements of `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` whose reduced norm has even $q$-adic valuation, and $\Gamma_2(\ell) = \Gamma_2(\mathrm{none}) \cap s_2(\ell)\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})s_2(\ell)^{-1}$. Elements $w_2$ and $\bar w_2$, again indexed by `Option`: $w_2(\mathrm{none})$ lies in `awayUnits R₁ v₂` and has reduced norm $q$, and $w_2(\ell)$ lies in `awayUnits (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) v₂` with reduced norm $q$; $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$ has reduced norm $q'$, its local image lies in the local box units of $R_1$ at every place $u \neq v_2$ not above $q'$, and conjugation by it preserves the local boxes of $R_1$ and of $\Lambda_1$ at every $u \neq v_2$, with the same three conditions for $\bar w_2(\ell)$ relative to `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)` and $\Lambda_1$.
--
--   Decomposition-group data. A homomorphism $dIso_2$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ to the isometric automorphisms of the completion, implementing the Galois action (hypothesis $hdIso_2$), and a quadratic character $\chi$ of that decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathbb{Z}/2$ which is trivial on inertia ($h\chi_1$), nontrivial on any Frobenius at $q$ ($h\chi_2$), and whose kernel consists exactly of those $\tau$ fixing every element of the residue field of $A_2$ satisfying $x^{q^2} = x$ ($h\chi_3$).
--
--   Integral and formal data. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}_0$ which is a discrete valuation ring, with irreducible $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, residue field of cardinality $q$, and $(q) = (\pi)$ (so absolutely unramified over $\mathbb{Z}_q$); $\mathcal{O}_0$ is an $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra inside the rational closure of $A_2$, of which the latter is the fraction field. An $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra $Onr$, a characteristic-zero domain, with an $\mathcal{O}_0$-automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, with $Onr$ integral over $\mathcal{O}_0$ modulo $\pi$ (hypothesis `hOa`), with all monic polynomials of positive degree having roots modulo $\pi$ (hypothesis `hOcl`), and with $Fr(x) \equiv x^q$ modulo $\pi$ (hypothesis `hFr`); so $Onr$ plays the role of the completed unramified closure together with its Frobenius. A determinant-valuation homomorphism `vdet` on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the rational closure, characterised by the condition `hvdet` that $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ precisely when $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_0$ times $\pi^n$. A ring map $\psi_0 : Onr \to$ the completion, with $\pi \mapsto \varpi_2.\varpi$ (`hπϖ`), $N$ a unit in $\mathcal{O}_0$ (`hN₀`), the image of $\mathcal{O}_0$ in the rational closure being exactly the elements of valuation $\le 1$ (`h𝒪₀`), $\psi_0$ taking values of valuation $\le 1$ (`hψ₀`), $\psi_0$ compatible with the two structure maps (`hψ₀𝒪`), and a rank-one condition `hrk` asserting that for $x$ of valuation $< 1$ and $y \neq 0$ some power of $v(x)$ is at most $v(y)$.
--
--   Integral coarse moduli and correspondences. A scheme $\mathcal{X}_0$ with $f_0 : \mathcal{X}_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ and a point-assignment $pt_0$ such that `IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳₀ f₀ pt₀` holds; $\mathcal{X}_0$ is integral and $f_0$ is flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact. For each prime $\ell \neq q,q'$ a scheme $\mathcal{Y}_0(\ell)$ with $g_0(\ell)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ and $ptT_0(\ell)$ making it a coarse moduli space `IsCoarseModuliT Λ N ℓ` for fake elliptic curves with extra level $\ell$; two degeneracy morphisms $d_{0}(\ell), d_{1}(\ell) : \mathcal{Y}_0(\ell) \to \mathcal{X}_0$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), the first sending the point of a level structure to the point of its underlying curve (`hd₀`), the second sending it to the point of any $\ell$-level isogenous quotient (`hd₁`). Two self-maps $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal{X}_0$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q$ and at $q'$ respectively (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation data. Functorial maps $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ from the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with the formal Drinfel'd functor `FormalOmega.Omega` (Deligne data on the lattice tree, over $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebras) to the nilpotent points of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$. The hypothesis `hCD` is a conjunction of nine groups of clauses, summarised here: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action (`FormalOmega.OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` with respect to $\pi$, $Onr$, $Fr$, `vdet`) of the image under $\iota_2$ of `awayUnits R₁ v₂`, and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ under that of `awayUnits R₁ v₂` intersected with its $s_2(\ell)$-conjugate; over algebraically closed $\pi$-nilpotent fields, surjectivity of $\Theta$ (respectively $\Theta T(\ell)$) in the second variable and the statement that two Deligne data have the same image exactly when they are related by the twisted action of such a $\gamma$; universality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$ among naturally twisted-invariant maps to nilpotent points of any scheme over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$, with uniqueness of the induced map; compatibility of $\Theta T(\ell)$ with $d_0(\ell)$ ($\Theta$ is recovered) and with $d_1(\ell)$ (after the twisted action of $s_2(\ell)$); and compatibility of $\Theta$ with $ar$ (Frobenius twist by $1$ in the first coordinate) and with $arbar$ (the twisted action of $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$).
--
--   Conclusion. Write $K_0$ for the rational closure of $A_2$, the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}_0$, and for a morphism $h$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ write $h_{K_0}$ for the second projection of the pullback of $h$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{O}_0 \to K_0$. Then four assertions hold: $f_{0,K_0}$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$; $f_{0,K_0}$ is geometrically connected; for every prime $\ell \neq q,q'$, $g_0(\ell)_{K_0}$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$; and for every such $\ell$, $g_0(\ell)_{K_0}$ is geometrically connected.
--
--   This supplies the geometric input on the generic fibres of the integral coarse moduli schemes of fake elliptic curves over the absolutely unramified discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_0$ at $q$: smoothness of relative dimension one and geometric connectedness, both for the Shimura curve itself and for each auxiliary curve with extra level structure $\ell$. It is used by the Mumford-embedding step [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd), where these properties are needed to pass from the formal Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation to the function field of the curve over $K_0$. The hypothesis frame is that of the uniformisation statement, retained verbatim.
